course: dictionary
lesson: 15692
title: Tiredly: showing how we feel
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Tiredly is an adverb. An adverb tells us how someone does something. It often ends in -ly, like quickly or happily. Tired is the adjective, and tiredly is the same idea used for an action.
explain: «She smiled tiredly at her mum.» The word tiredly tells us how she smiled. Her smile was slow and weak, because she had very little energy left after a long day.
explain: Tiredly means in a tired way, showing that you have little energy. Look for clues around it, such as yawning, sitting down or a long day, to help you spot when the word is used.
fact: Tiredly is an adverb, so it describes how someone does something.
fact: Tiredly means in a tired way, showing that you have little energy.
fact: «Tired» is an adjective, and «tiredly» is the adverb form that describes an action.
fact: «He stretched tiredly and went to bed» tells us he was worn out.
fact: A good check is to swap in your meaning: «She sat down wearily» still makes sense, so tiredly means in a tired way.
exercise: «The baby rubbed her eyes and yawned tiredly.» What does tiredly mean? | In a loud, angry way | In a happy, bouncy way | *In a tired way, with little energy | In a fast, running way
exercise: «Sam walked tiredly home after the long hike.» Which word tells how Sam walked? | hike | Sam | *tiredly
exercise: «Ben said tiredly, "Can we stop now?"» Why might the author use tiredly? | Because Ben was shouting across a field | Because Ben was singing a song | *Because Ben had little energy left | Because Ben was jumping for joy
test: «The girl put down her bag tiredly and sat on the step.» What does tiredly show? | *She has little energy | She is very excited | She is running fast
test: Which word is the adverb that means in a tired way? | *tiredly | tiredness | sleepy | tired
exam: Read: «He stretched tiredly and went to bed.» What does tiredly tell us? | He was singing a song | *He was worn out and had little energy | He was running a race | He was excited about the party
